1
00:00:01,626 --> 00:00:04,129
[POLICE OFFICER]
<i>You can count on us. Don't worry.</i>

2
00:00:04,212 --> 00:00:06,715
<i>We will do our best.</i>

3
00:00:07,549 --> 00:00:11,136
<i>You know, that's what you guys always say.</i>

4
00:00:12,178 --> 00:00:14,055
<i>But nothing ever happens.</i>

5
00:00:14,556 --> 00:00:18,393
<i>We won't have any peace</i>
<i>until that Billy leaves us alone!</i>

6
00:00:18,476 --> 00:00:19,561
<i>Look, if you want--</i>

7
00:00:19,644 --> 00:00:20,603
[BEA] <i>Uh, Ma…</i>

8
00:00:21,521 --> 00:00:25,066
<i>What I want</i>
<i>is for you to let me deal with Billy.</i>

9
00:00:25,734 --> 00:00:27,152
<i>I'll handle her, okay?</i>

10
00:00:27,235 --> 00:00:28,319
<i>I can handle her.</i>

11
00:00:28,403 --> 00:00:30,822
[JORDAN]<i> Buddy,</i>
<i>your sister loves you so much.</i>

12
00:00:30,905 --> 00:00:32,282
<i>That's why she did that.</i>

13
00:00:32,365 --> 00:00:34,909
<i>Of course you would side with Billy.</i>

14
00:00:34,993 --> 00:00:36,536
<i>I'm not siding with anyone.</i>

15
00:00:36,619 --> 00:00:38,038
<i>Bro Dude,</i>

16
00:00:38,121 --> 00:00:42,250
<i>didn't you say your father left you too?</i>

17
00:00:42,333 --> 00:00:44,586
<i>If he came back and reached out to you,</i>

18
00:00:44,669 --> 00:00:47,255
<i>wouldn't you want to talk to him?</i>

19
00:00:47,338 --> 00:00:50,884
[DINO]<i> Family is</i>
<i>the Lord's most important gift.</i>

20
00:00:50,967 --> 00:00:53,094
<i>I deeply regret</i>

21
00:00:53,178 --> 00:00:55,055
<i>what I did to my children</i>

22
00:00:55,638 --> 00:00:57,057
<i>and to my wife.</i>

23
00:00:57,766 --> 00:00:59,809
<i>But I believe</i>

24
00:00:59,893 --> 00:01:00,977
<i>that it is not too late.</i>

25
00:01:01,061 --> 00:01:02,437
<i>Amen.</i>

26
00:01:04,314 --> 00:01:05,356
[JORDAN] <i>He just needs time.</i>

27
00:01:06,441 --> 00:01:07,609
<i>Am I wrong?</i>

28
00:01:10,820 --> 00:01:13,615
<i>I mean, we're the same.</i>

29
00:01:14,491 --> 00:01:16,326
<i>I still can't forgive my dad either.</i>

30
00:01:18,495 --> 00:01:19,788
<i>But you love Oliver.</i>

31
00:01:20,413 --> 00:01:21,748
<i>That's all that matters.</i>

32
00:01:23,583 --> 00:01:25,293
[BEA] <i>I hesitated at first, Abi.</i>

33
00:01:25,376 --> 00:01:27,253
<i>I wasn't sure if</i>

34
00:01:27,337 --> 00:01:29,589
<i>it was really Papa I saw in the video.</i>

35
00:01:29,672 --> 00:01:31,883
<i>I went to Billy's house.</i>

36
00:01:31,966 --> 00:01:34,677
<i>He went to see Billy first,</i>

37
00:01:35,553 --> 00:01:38,181
<i>before even coming to his own family.</i>

38
00:01:38,264 --> 00:01:40,892
<i>…listening to our favorite song</i>
<i>during the trip.</i>

39
00:01:40,975 --> 00:01:42,393
<i>What was it again?</i>

40
00:01:42,477 --> 00:01:45,021
<i>- I don't know. You tell me.</i>
- [LAUGHTER]

41
00:01:45,104 --> 00:01:46,648
<i>Who's going to sing it?</i>

42
00:01:46,731 --> 00:01:49,442
<i>- I will! I'm the singer!</i>
<i>- Okay, okay, okay.</i>

43
00:01:49,526 --> 00:01:50,944
- [MARIELA] <i>All right.</i>
<i>- Take the lead. Go!</i>

44
00:01:51,027 --> 00:01:53,404
<i>What are we to him?</i>

45
00:01:56,241 --> 00:01:57,742
<i>Trash?</i>

46
00:02:00,411 --> 00:02:01,579
<i>Trash.</i>

47
00:02:02,539 --> 00:02:04,624
<i>That's all we are to him.</i>

48
00:02:05,250 --> 00:02:07,085
[MARIELA]
<i>Your father has abandoned us.</i>

49
00:02:07,168 --> 00:02:09,295
<i>He has a new family in Manila.</i>

50
00:02:09,379 --> 00:02:13,591
He cheated on me. He cheated on us!

51
00:02:13,675 --> 00:02:16,511
<i>He chose his mistress</i>

52
00:02:17,262 --> 00:02:19,597
<i>and their illegitimate child!</i>

53
00:02:19,681 --> 00:02:22,851
<i>They are to blame for your sister's death!</i>

54
00:02:23,434 --> 00:02:26,688
<i>Damn them. Damn all of them!</i>

55
00:02:26,771 --> 00:02:29,941
<i>Damn them!</i>

56
00:02:33,736 --> 00:02:40,410
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

57
00:03:25,163 --> 00:03:26,331
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

58
00:03:26,414 --> 00:03:33,296
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

59
00:03:38,134 --> 00:03:39,469
<i>That's all good now, sir.</i>

60
00:03:43,473 --> 00:03:44,557
<i>Uh, sir…</i>

61
00:03:45,141 --> 00:03:48,728
<i>About the advance pay I was asking for…</i>

62
00:03:48,811 --> 00:03:51,022
<i>Could I please receive it today?</i>

63
00:03:51,105 --> 00:03:57,237
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

64
00:03:57,320 --> 00:04:00,531
<i>This is the last time I'll do this, okay?</i>
<i>I'm making a loss because of you!</i>

65
00:04:03,952 --> 00:04:05,828
<i>I'm sorry, sir.</i>

66
00:04:07,247 --> 00:04:09,332
<i>It's just that my mother</i>
<i>still hasn't recovered.</i>

67
00:04:09,415 --> 00:04:11,626
<i>She keeps going back to the hospital.</i>

68
00:04:12,210 --> 00:04:13,336
[MAN SIGHS DEEPLY]

69
00:04:13,419 --> 00:04:14,879
<i>It might be better for your mother</i>

70
00:04:14,963 --> 00:04:17,382
<i>if she just returns to your hometown.</i>

71
00:04:19,259 --> 00:04:20,927
<i>Even if I wanted to,</i>

72
00:04:21,511 --> 00:04:23,137
<i>we have nothing to go back to there.</i>

73
00:04:23,221 --> 00:04:25,348
<i>We already sold our property there</i>

74
00:04:25,431 --> 00:04:29,060
<i>and used that money</i>
<i>to pay for hospital bills.</i>

75
00:04:29,143 --> 00:04:31,187
<i>And where is your father?</i>

76
00:04:31,271 --> 00:04:34,023
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

77
00:04:34,107 --> 00:04:35,233
[MAN SIGHS]

78
00:04:35,316 --> 00:04:37,819
<i>Okay, I'll get going. Look after the shop.</i>

79
00:04:49,122 --> 00:04:56,129
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

80
00:05:09,475 --> 00:05:12,061
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

81
00:05:12,145 --> 00:05:13,646
[YOUNG BILLY GIGGLING]

82
00:05:13,730 --> 00:05:17,650
<i>- You bought a lot, huh?</i>
<i>- Daddy! </i>[GIGGLES]

83
00:05:17,734 --> 00:05:19,444
- [OLIVE] <i>My goodness.</i>
<i>- Pa?</i>

84
00:05:19,527 --> 00:05:22,030
- [OLIVE] <i>She's such a daddy's girl!</i>
- [ENRICO] <i>Are you happy now?</i>

85
00:05:22,113 --> 00:05:24,157
- [YOUNG BILLY] <i>Yes. Thank you, Daddy.</i>
<i>- Pa?</i>

86
00:05:24,240 --> 00:05:25,074
[WOMAN] <i>Oh!</i>

87
00:05:25,158 --> 00:05:27,869
- [ENRICO] <i>Okay, let's go.</i>
- [WOMAN] <i>Watch where you're going.</i>

88
00:05:27,952 --> 00:05:29,871
[OLIVE] <i>Come on, let's hurry up.</i>

89
00:05:29,954 --> 00:05:32,332
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

90
00:05:32,415 --> 00:05:33,416
<i>Pa?</i>

91
00:05:34,125 --> 00:05:35,877
[OLIVE] <i>Wear your seat belt, dear.</i>

92
00:05:35,960 --> 00:05:37,879
[YOUNG BILLY GIGGLING] <i>Yes.</i>

93
00:05:37,962 --> 00:05:39,464
- [OLIVE] <i>We're so happy.</i>
- [BEA] <i>Pa.</i>

94
00:05:39,547 --> 00:05:41,716
<i>Pa. Pa!</i>

95
00:05:41,799 --> 00:05:42,884
<i>Pa!</i>

96
00:05:44,343 --> 00:05:45,470
<i>Pa.</i>

97
00:05:48,639 --> 00:05:49,891
<i>Pa.</i>

98
00:05:49,974 --> 00:05:51,768
<i>Pa!</i>

99
00:05:52,852 --> 00:05:56,773
[BEA SOBBING]

100
00:05:56,856 --> 00:06:02,570
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

101
00:06:04,155 --> 00:06:05,907
[KEYBOARD CLACKING]

102
00:06:07,408 --> 00:06:14,415
[MUSIC TURNS FOREBODING]

103
00:06:29,388 --> 00:06:36,395
[FOREBODING MUSIC CONTINUES]

104
00:06:53,412 --> 00:06:58,668
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

105
00:07:15,435 --> 00:07:20,982
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

106
00:07:33,411 --> 00:07:36,998
[APPLAUSE]

107
00:07:40,209 --> 00:07:45,756
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

108
00:07:54,432 --> 00:07:59,937
<i>…we are preparing something</i>
<i>bigger and better for LoveList.</i>

109
00:08:00,771 --> 00:08:04,859
<i>And I'm sure that here, love is better,</i>

110
00:08:04,942 --> 00:08:06,861
<i>whether it's the first</i>
<i>or second time around,</i>

111
00:08:06,944 --> 00:08:09,655
<i>as long as you are with the right one…</i>

112
00:08:09,739 --> 00:08:12,200
[CROWD] <i>At the right time!</i>

113
00:08:12,283 --> 00:08:14,535
[CROWD CHEERING]

114
00:08:14,619 --> 00:08:16,078
[WOMAN] <i>Yeah!</i>

115
00:08:16,162 --> 00:08:18,164
<i>Congratulations!</i>

116
00:08:18,247 --> 00:08:22,335
<i>Happy anniversary to us, LoveList!</i>

117
00:08:22,418 --> 00:08:24,795
[CHEERING, APPLAUDING]

118
00:08:24,879 --> 00:08:26,130
<i>Let's go, let's go!</i>

119
00:08:26,214 --> 00:08:30,384
[BILLY] <i>And because we are celebrating</i>
<i>our second anniversary,</i>

120
00:08:30,468 --> 00:08:35,973
<i>we are preparing something</i>
<i>bigger and better for LoveList.</i>

121
00:08:37,141 --> 00:08:41,062
<i>And I'm sure that here, love is better,</i>

122
00:08:41,145 --> 00:08:43,231
<i>whether it's the first</i>
<i>or second time around</i>

123
00:08:43,314 --> 00:08:46,025
<i>only if you're with the right one.</i>

124
00:08:46,108 --> 00:08:48,569
<i>- At the right time!</i>
<i>- At the right time!</i>

125
00:08:48,653 --> 00:08:52,240
- [CHEERS AND CLAPPING IN VIDEO]
- [BILLY] <i>Happy anniversary!</i>

126
00:08:52,323 --> 00:08:54,242
[AUDIENCE CHEERING]

127
00:08:54,325 --> 00:08:55,743
[BILLY] <i>Yay!</i>

128
00:08:55,826 --> 00:09:00,831
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

129
00:09:00,915 --> 00:09:07,922
[MUSIC BECOMES EERIE]

130
00:09:18,349 --> 00:09:25,064
[SPRAY PAINT HISSING, RATTLING]

131
00:09:25,147 --> 00:09:26,274
[VALERIE] <i>Hello, mister?</i>

132
00:09:27,108 --> 00:09:30,111
<i>Hello, mister? Where are you?</i>

133
00:09:30,194 --> 00:09:32,738
<i>I've been waiting for you!</i>
<i>Please hurry up.</i>

134
00:09:32,822 --> 00:09:39,829
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

135
00:09:55,386 --> 00:10:00,308
[FOREBODING MUSIC CONTINUES, FADES]

136
00:10:00,933 --> 00:10:02,268
[MOUTHS SILENTLY]

137
00:10:03,311 --> 00:10:09,233
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

138
00:10:24,915 --> 00:10:27,335
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC FADES]

139
00:10:27,418 --> 00:10:28,294
<i>Let's eat.</i>

140
00:10:28,377 --> 00:10:29,879
<i>Oh, where's Oliver?</i>

141
00:10:29,962 --> 00:10:31,464
<i>He's already sleeping.</i>

142
00:10:31,547 --> 00:10:33,424
<i>Then why are there three plates?</i>

143
00:10:33,507 --> 00:10:35,134
<i>Didn't you see my message?</i>

144
00:10:35,217 --> 00:10:37,261
<i>We have a visitor.</i>

145
00:10:37,345 --> 00:10:39,805
<i>- Who?</i>
- [PRECIOUS] <i>Just there.</i>

146
00:10:39,889 --> 00:10:43,517
<i>- Come.</i>
<i>- Ms. Billy! Hello!</i>

147
00:10:43,601 --> 00:10:44,560
<i>Abi!</i>

148
00:10:44,644 --> 00:10:47,813
<i>I went to the center earlier.</i>

149
00:10:47,897 --> 00:10:50,316
<i>I just wanted to thank you</i>

150
00:10:50,399 --> 00:10:53,694
<i>because our conversation</i>
<i>really helped me a lot.</i>

151
00:10:53,778 --> 00:10:54,904
[BILLY] <i>Mm…</i>

152
00:10:54,987 --> 00:10:56,572
<i>But you weren't there,</i>

153
00:10:56,656 --> 00:11:00,743
<i>so Ms. Precious became</i>
<i>the victim of my endless talking.</i>

154
00:11:00,826 --> 00:11:03,496
<i>That's why I brought her with me.</i>

155
00:11:03,579 --> 00:11:04,955
[BILLY] <i>I'm sorry, Auntie Pres.</i>

156
00:11:05,831 --> 00:11:09,710
<i>I'm just mad at people</i>
<i>who can't fight without hiding.</i>

157
00:11:10,378 --> 00:11:13,381
<i>I can't just let them get away with this.</i>

158
00:11:13,464 --> 00:11:17,051
<i>The moment I find out</i>
<i>who started all this,</i>

159
00:11:17,134 --> 00:11:20,554
<i>I'll do everything I can</i>
<i>to put them in jail.</i>

160
00:11:20,638 --> 00:11:22,515
<i>They don't know</i>
<i>what I'm like when I'm angry.</i>

161
00:11:24,725 --> 00:11:26,894
<i>- I'm sorry, Abi.</i>
- [BEA] <i>Hmm?</i>

162
00:11:27,686 --> 00:11:28,854
<i>I'm sorry about this.</i>

163
00:11:29,897 --> 00:11:32,525
<i>I'm not really good at handling my anger.</i>

164
00:11:32,608 --> 00:11:36,487
<i>Oh, Ms. Billy, don't worry about me.</i>

165
00:11:36,570 --> 00:11:37,822
<i>I'm perfectly fine.</i>

166
00:11:37,905 --> 00:11:42,701
<i>If I could,</i>
<i>I'd help you in any way possible.</i>

167
00:11:42,785 --> 00:11:44,662
<i>And I mean, anything.</i>

168
00:11:46,831 --> 00:11:49,625
<i>Enough of that. Come on and eat.</i>

169
00:11:49,708 --> 00:11:51,669
<i>You haven't even taken a bite.</i>

170
00:11:51,752 --> 00:11:53,587
[PRECIOUS] <i>Keep eating, dear.</i>

171
00:11:53,671 --> 00:11:55,297
<i>Come on.</i>

172
00:11:55,381 --> 00:11:56,757
<i>Hey.</i>

173
00:11:58,300 --> 00:11:59,176
<i>Okay.</i>

174
00:11:59,260 --> 00:12:05,683
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

175
00:12:20,906 --> 00:12:27,371
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES,
THEN FADES]

176
00:12:35,212 --> 00:12:36,422
Auntie Pres?

177
00:12:38,132 --> 00:12:39,258
Still nothing?

178
00:12:39,842 --> 00:12:41,260
I already called him.

179
00:12:41,886 --> 00:12:45,014
He's still in his room.
Still refusing to eat.

180
00:12:45,097 --> 00:12:48,392
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

181
00:12:48,476 --> 00:12:51,812
Auntie, I understand why
he would feel this way.

182
00:12:53,022 --> 00:12:55,649
But I can't give him what he wants.

183
00:12:58,527 --> 00:13:00,404
I'll just bring him food upstairs.

184
00:13:02,615 --> 00:13:03,574
I'll do it.

185
00:13:03,657 --> 00:13:10,664
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

186
00:13:15,711 --> 00:13:21,842
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

187
00:13:26,931 --> 00:13:29,183
[MARIELA] <i>Sweetie! Let's eat!</i>

188
00:13:32,436 --> 00:13:33,521
Coming, Ma!

189
00:13:33,604 --> 00:13:40,569
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

190
00:13:49,036 --> 00:13:51,163
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

191
00:13:54,667 --> 00:13:55,918
[THUDS SOFTLY]

192
00:13:56,961 --> 00:13:58,045
Lunch's ready.

193
00:14:07,888 --> 00:14:08,973
Eat up.

194
00:14:09,557 --> 00:14:11,141
Skipping meals isn't good for you.

195
00:14:11,225 --> 00:14:16,564
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

196
00:14:16,647 --> 00:14:18,148
How's your sugar level?

197
00:14:22,444 --> 00:14:23,863
Come on, Oliver.

198
00:14:23,946 --> 00:14:25,114
Eat your meal.

199
00:14:29,535 --> 00:14:30,661
Oliver.

200
00:14:31,662 --> 00:14:33,414
Please eat.

201
00:14:34,039 --> 00:14:36,750
Let me speak to Papa first.

202
00:14:43,048 --> 00:14:45,259
Do you want to be hospitalized again?

203
00:14:48,178 --> 00:14:50,556
Not to mention,
the person you want to talk to

204
00:14:50,639 --> 00:14:53,183
is the one who passed on
that disease to you.

205
00:14:55,102 --> 00:14:57,313
That's not his fault.

206
00:15:00,357 --> 00:15:04,111
You were just a baby when it happened,
so you can't remember it.

207
00:15:06,196 --> 00:15:09,116
But that man you think is kind to you

208
00:15:09,199 --> 00:15:12,036
is the reason our mother died.

209
00:15:12,620 --> 00:15:14,705
Why we almost got separated.

210
00:15:14,788 --> 00:15:16,832
Why we had to live on the streets.

211
00:15:18,792 --> 00:15:21,337
All of that happened
because he abandoned us.

212
00:15:21,420 --> 00:15:28,302
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

213
00:15:31,931 --> 00:15:35,225
I don't think I could handle it
if something bad happened to you.

214
00:15:45,986 --> 00:15:47,071
Oliver!

215
00:15:47,655 --> 00:15:49,031
- Are you dizzy?
- Billy.

216
00:15:49,114 --> 00:15:50,908
- Check his sugar level.
- Okay.

217
00:15:51,617 --> 00:15:52,618
[PRECIOUS] Stay there.

218
00:15:52,701 --> 00:15:56,205
[RUSTLING]

219
00:16:02,544 --> 00:16:03,504
Ready?

220
00:16:06,173 --> 00:16:07,049
[CLICKS]

221
00:16:07,132 --> 00:16:12,680
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

222
00:16:16,016 --> 00:16:17,351
[MONITOR BEEPS]

223
00:16:19,061 --> 00:16:20,938
[RUSTLING]

224
00:16:21,897 --> 00:16:23,232
- [CLINKS]
- Have a drink first,

225
00:16:23,315 --> 00:16:24,775
and then eat a lot, okay?

226
00:16:24,858 --> 00:16:27,486
[JUICE TRICKLING]

227
00:16:27,569 --> 00:16:28,654
Go on.

228
00:16:29,905 --> 00:16:31,115
[CLINKS]

229
00:16:34,118 --> 00:16:35,035
Okay.

230
00:16:35,119 --> 00:16:41,333
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

231
00:16:48,674 --> 00:16:49,633
Grandpa.

232
00:16:50,384 --> 00:16:51,385
I have some good news.

233
00:16:51,468 --> 00:16:54,096
I'm moving you to a better facility.

234
00:16:54,680 --> 00:16:55,681
Somewhere nicer

235
00:16:55,764 --> 00:16:56,974
and bigger.

236
00:16:57,641 --> 00:16:59,518
That's good news, right?

237
00:16:59,601 --> 00:17:01,270
Sir Jordan.

238
00:17:01,353 --> 00:17:03,689
You need to sign a few papers
for the transfer.

239
00:17:03,772 --> 00:17:05,983
- Okay. Grandpa?
- This way, please.

240
00:17:06,984 --> 00:17:08,152
I'll be back, okay?

241
00:17:09,486 --> 00:17:11,822
[DOOR CREAKS]

242
00:17:11,905 --> 00:17:13,323
[DOOR CLICKS]

243
00:17:16,869 --> 00:17:22,499
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

244
00:17:30,424 --> 00:17:31,467
Dude.

245
00:17:33,052 --> 00:17:34,094
[JORDAN] Dude?

246
00:17:35,387 --> 00:17:36,889
Oliver's still mad.

247
00:17:36,972 --> 00:17:39,224
- Sir Jordan, your grandpa…
- What's wrong?

248
00:17:39,308 --> 00:17:42,102
He escaped.
But security is already looking for him.

249
00:17:42,186 --> 00:17:43,062
What?!

250
00:17:43,812 --> 00:17:45,189
Jordan?

251
00:17:45,272 --> 00:17:46,607
Are you okay?

252
00:17:47,191 --> 00:17:49,068
Sorry. My grandpa is missing.

253
00:17:49,151 --> 00:17:50,152
What?!

254
00:17:50,861 --> 00:17:52,488
All right, I'm on my way.

255
00:17:53,906 --> 00:17:55,074
- Hurry up.
- Okay, sir.

256
00:17:55,157 --> 00:17:57,159
Why were you being so careless?!

257
00:17:57,242 --> 00:17:58,827
- I'm so sorry.
- This shouldn't be happening.

258
00:17:58,911 --> 00:18:00,579
We're responsible for this.

259
00:18:00,662 --> 00:18:01,789
- I told you--
- Well?

260
00:18:01,872 --> 00:18:03,165
You still haven't found my grandpa?!

261
00:18:03,248 --> 00:18:04,917
Sir, we're very, very sorry.

262
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:07,711
But we're still looking for him.
We are looking for him, sir.

263
00:18:07,795 --> 00:18:10,089
- I'm sorry.
- Sir, I'll help out too.

264
00:18:10,172 --> 00:18:11,590
No!

265
00:18:11,673 --> 00:18:12,966
Just stay away!

266
00:18:13,050 --> 00:18:14,051
[NURSE] No one's picking up.

267
00:18:14,134 --> 00:18:15,094
Go!

268
00:18:15,177 --> 00:18:19,306
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

269
00:18:19,389 --> 00:18:20,474
This shouldn't be happening!

270
00:18:23,477 --> 00:18:24,436
Excuse me.

271
00:18:25,354 --> 00:18:26,480
Have you seen this man?

272
00:18:26,563 --> 00:18:27,689
- No.
- No.

273
00:18:27,773 --> 00:18:28,816
- Are you sure?
- Yes.

274
00:18:30,526 --> 00:18:31,568
All right.

275
00:18:33,529 --> 00:18:36,073
Excuse me.
Can you help me? Ah…

276
00:18:36,156 --> 00:18:37,366
Have you seen him?

277
00:18:37,449 --> 00:18:39,993
- No. I haven't.
- No?

278
00:18:40,077 --> 00:18:41,495
- Are you sure?
- Yes, I'm sure.

279
00:18:41,578 --> 00:18:42,871
All right, thank you.

280
00:18:42,955 --> 00:18:47,543
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

281
00:18:47,626 --> 00:18:48,669
Jordan!

282
00:18:48,752 --> 00:18:50,963
Dude, I can't find him!

283
00:18:51,964 --> 00:18:53,549
Please, I can't lose him too.

284
00:18:53,632 --> 00:18:54,758
Jordan, breathe.

285
00:18:54,842 --> 00:18:55,926
Breathe.

286
00:18:56,009 --> 00:18:57,261
[INHALES, EXHALES SHARPLY]

287
00:18:57,344 --> 00:18:58,887
We'll find him, okay?

288
00:18:58,971 --> 00:19:01,265
Let's split up so we can find him faster.

289
00:19:01,348 --> 00:19:02,474
I'll go this way, you go that way.

290
00:19:02,558 --> 00:19:04,852
Breathe. We'll find him.

291
00:19:04,935 --> 00:19:05,811
Let's go.

292
00:19:05,894 --> 00:19:12,151
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

293
00:19:12,234 --> 00:19:14,069
<i>My life became worthless.</i>

294
00:19:14,153 --> 00:19:16,280
<i>But everything changed</i>
<i>when I met this girl.</i>

295
00:19:16,363 --> 00:19:18,407
<i>But sadly, I can't be with her.</i>

296
00:19:18,490 --> 00:19:19,700
<i>What do you know?</i>

297
00:19:19,783 --> 00:19:23,662
<i>Your brother is throwing a tantrum,</i>
<i>insisting on going to school.</i>

298
00:19:23,745 --> 00:19:25,122
[BILLY] <i>Auntie, where's Oliver?</i>

299
00:19:25,205 --> 00:19:26,123
<i>Pa?</i>

300
00:19:27,749 --> 00:19:29,042
<i>Why did you leave us?</i>

301
00:19:29,543 --> 00:19:31,587
[BEA] <i>I will avenge us.</i>

302
00:19:31,670 --> 00:19:35,591
<i>I will avenge us both, okay?</i>

303
00:19:35,674 --> 00:19:39,469
[MARIELA] <i>That devil-spawn father of yours</i>
<i>is together with Billy's aunt!</i>

304
00:19:39,553 --> 00:19:40,971
<i>I'll kill them!</i>

305
00:19:41,054 --> 00:19:42,472
<i>I'll kill them both!</i>

306
00:19:42,556 --> 00:19:44,183
<i>I'll kill them!</i>

307
00:19:44,266 --> 00:19:47,394
<i>- Enrico, let's meet. We need to talk.</i>
<i>- Okay.</i>

308
00:19:47,853 --> 00:19:52,524
<i>People who deceive and steal</i>
<i>deserve to die.</i>

309
00:19:52,608 --> 00:19:54,443
<i>- This is for my daughter!</i>
<i>- Enough, Mariela!</i>

310
00:19:54,526 --> 00:19:55,569
[PRECIOUS] <i>Mariela!</i>

311
00:19:55,652 --> 00:19:59,573
- [MAN] <i>You're a feisty one, I see.</i>
<i>- Mm-hmm. Get it.</i>

312
00:19:59,656 --> 00:20:02,534
[BILLY] <i>Good thing I'm here, right?</i>

313
00:20:02,618 --> 00:20:04,494
<i>What would you do without me?</i>

314
00:20:05,037 --> 00:20:06,538
[JORDAN] <i>We've known</i>
<i>each other for so long.</i>

315
00:20:06,622 --> 00:20:08,290
<i>I can't help</i>

316
00:20:08,373 --> 00:20:09,333
<i>but fall.</i>

317
00:20:09,958 --> 00:20:12,127
<i>So let me take this chance to say,</i>

318
00:20:12,211 --> 00:20:13,462
<i>I think I love you.</i>
